# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values. Never commit .env.
#
# IMPORTANT: there is currently only ONE Supabase database (this one) --
# no separate test project exists yet. `npm run test:db` runs against
# DATABASE_URL/DIRECT_URL, the SAME connection strings as the app, with
# every test wrapped in a transaction that is always rolled back (see
# tests/db/helpers.ts#inRollbackTx and tests/db/global-setup.ts).
# Revisit before production go-live: provision a dedicated test/staging
# Supabase project instead of testing against the real one.

# --- App runtime -------------------------------------------------------

NODE_ENV=development

# fatal | error | warn | info | debug | trace | silent
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Supabase POOLER connection (Supavisor, TRANSACTION mode, port 6543).
# Used at runtime and by `prisma migrate deploy`. Authenticates as the
# restricted role `fsj_app`, never as the project owner.
#
# Username format for the pooler is `fsj_app.<project-ref>` (Supabase
# requires the project ref suffix on pooled connections) -- find
# <project-ref> in your Supabase project URL/settings.
# `pgbouncer=true` disables Prisma's prepared-statement caching, required
# when the pooler is in transaction mode.
#
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://fsj_app.<project-ref>:<FSJ_APP_DB_PASSWORD>@<host>:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true"

# Supabase DIRECT connection (bypasses the pooler), owner role `postgres`.
# Used ONLY for `prisma migrate dev` / `migrate diff` and by
# scripts/db-bootstrap.ts. Never used at runtime.
#
# DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres:<owner-password>@<host>:5432/postgres"

# Password to set for the `fsj_app` role. Used only by
# `npm run db:bootstrap` (scripts/db-bootstrap.ts); never logged, never
# embedded in a migration file. Generate a strong random value.
# FSJ_APP_DB_PASSWORD="<generate-a-strong-random-password>"

# --- DB test harness (tests/db/**, `npm run test:db`) -------------------
#
# Runs against the SAME database as DATABASE_URL/DIRECT_URL above --
# there is no separate test project. Safety comes from every test running
# inside a transaction that is always rolled back, never from a separate
# database. Explicit opt-in required (must be exactly "yes") because these
# tests connect to the real database, even though nothing persists.
# FSJ_DB_TESTS=yes

# --- Daily jobs (app/api/jobs/**) --------------------------------------
#
# FASE 12 point 12.2 (M15), extended FASE 14 point 14.5: shared secret for
# `GET|POST /api/jobs/plazos-archivo` (moves EN_ARCHIVO lotes de archivo to
# PLAZO_CUMPLIDO once their retention period, DP-26 PARCIAL, is met).
# Compared in constant time. Optional: if unset, the route answers 503
# instead of running. Generate a strong random value (Vercel recommends at
# least 16 random characters); never commit it.
#
# Two callers, same secret:
#  - Vercel Cron (`vercel.json`'s `crons` entry) sends GET with
#    `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>` -- set automatically by Vercel
#    from this SAME env var name when it invokes the cron path, see
#    https://vercel.com/docs/cron-jobs/manage-cron-jobs#securing-cron-jobs.
#  - Any other caller (manual trigger, a host cron outside Vercel) can use
#    POST with an `x-cron-secret: <CRON_SECRET>` header instead.
# CRON_SECRET="<generate-a-strong-random-secret>"
